<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Technical university</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as technical universities</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A technical university is a higher education institution specialising in engineering, applied sciences and technology. In nineteenth-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> a dense network of such institutions trained engineers and chemists for industry. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> credit these technical universities with producing the applied scientific capacity that sustained German industrial dominance before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p></div>
